1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,347
A whale swims like a fish.

2
00:00:02,347 --> 00:00:04,146
A bat flies like a bird.

3
00:00:04,146 --> 00:00:06,143
A penguin cannot fly at all.

4
00:00:06,543 --> 00:00:08,186
So is the whale a fish?

5
00:00:08,186 --> 00:00:09,540
Is the bat a bird?

6
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,612
And is the penguin even a bird?

7
00:00:12,062 --> 00:00:16,223
Diya's little cousin sorted them by
where they live and how they move.

8
00:00:16,223 --> 00:00:18,804
Diya said: every one of those is wrong.

9
00:00:19,154 --> 00:00:21,485
These animals break the obvious rule.

10
00:00:21,485 --> 00:00:23,389
And NEET loves to test them.

11
00:00:23,889 --> 00:00:28,228
By the end, you will know the one sure
mark of each class, and how to place

12
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:30,492
the odd ones that fool almost everyone.

13
00:00:31,142 --> 00:00:32,623
Here is the big idea.

14
00:00:32,623 --> 00:00:36,149
Where an animal lives, and
how it moves, can fool you.

15
00:00:36,499 --> 00:00:38,865
So we look at features that never lie.

16
00:00:38,865 --> 00:00:40,853
For each class, one sure mark.

17
00:00:41,303 --> 00:00:43,200
Fishes: fins and gills.

18
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:46,044
Amphibians: moist skin with no scales.

19
00:00:46,044 --> 00:00:48,834
Reptiles: dry skin covered in scales.

20
00:00:49,284 --> 00:00:50,470
Birds: feathers.

21
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:51,908
Only birds have them.

22
00:00:51,908 --> 00:00:55,793
Mammals: mammary glands that
make milk, and hair on the skin.

23
00:00:56,443 --> 00:01:00,308
Let's run the odd ones through a
sorting key, one gate at a time.

24
00:01:00,658 --> 00:01:01,558
Step one.

25
00:01:01,459 --> 00:01:02,611
The blue whale.

26
00:01:02,611 --> 00:01:07,053
It lives in the sea, but it breathes
with lungs and feeds its young on

27
00:01:07,053 --> 00:01:07,953
milk.

28
00:01:07,599 --> 00:01:08,499
Mammalia.

29
00:01:09,091 --> 00:01:09,991
Step two.

30
00:01:09,916 --> 00:01:10,816
The bat.

31
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,822
It flies, but it has hair,
outer ears, and mammary glands.

32
00:01:14,822 --> 00:01:17,396
NCERT names Pteropus, the flying fox.

33
00:01:17,396 --> 00:01:18,296
Mammalia.

34
00:01:18,910 --> 00:01:19,826
Step three.

35
00:01:19,826 --> 00:01:20,791
The penguin.

36
00:01:20,791 --> 00:01:23,140
It cannot fly, and swims instead.

37
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,350
But it has feathers and a beak.

38
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:26,250
Aves.

39
00:01:26,657 --> 00:01:27,573
Step four.

40
00:01:27,573 --> 00:01:29,615
The flying fish, Exocoetus.

41
00:01:29,615 --> 00:01:34,437
It glides above the waves, yet it
has fins, gills and an operculum.

42
00:01:34,437 --> 00:01:35,521
A bony fish.

43
00:01:36,271 --> 00:01:37,171
Step five.

44
00:01:37,163 --> 00:01:38,095
Ichthyophis.

45
00:01:38,095 --> 00:01:41,068
No legs at all, like a worm or a snake.

46
00:01:41,068 --> 00:01:43,281
But it is a limbless amphibian.

47
00:01:44,031 --> 00:01:44,931
Step six.

48
00:01:44,922 --> 00:01:47,127
The platypus, Ornithorhynchus.

49
00:01:47,127 --> 00:01:48,301
It lays eggs!

50
00:01:48,301 --> 00:01:50,930
Yet it has hair and mammary glands.

51
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:51,830
A mammal.

52
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:54,454
Two flyers, side by side.

53
00:01:54,454 --> 00:01:55,915
A bat and a crow.

54
00:01:56,265 --> 00:01:57,522
The bat has hair.

55
00:01:57,522 --> 00:01:59,014
The crow has feathers.

56
00:01:59,464 --> 00:02:01,907
The bat has outer ears, called pinnae.

57
00:02:01,907 --> 00:02:03,179
The crow has none.

58
00:02:03,629 --> 00:02:06,631
The bat gives birth to
young and feeds them milk.

59
00:02:06,631 --> 00:02:07,940
The crow lays eggs.

60
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,490
Your turn.

61
00:02:09,461 --> 00:02:12,861
A dolphin lives in the sea
and swims with flippers.

62
00:02:12,861 --> 00:02:14,191
Fish, or mammal?

63
00:02:14,191 --> 00:02:15,471
Pause and decide.

64
00:02:18,671 --> 00:02:19,571
Mammal!

65
00:02:19,328 --> 00:02:23,138
NCERT lists Delphinus, the
common dolphin, under Mammalia.

66
00:02:23,138 --> 00:02:26,521
It breathes with lungs and
feeds its young on milk.

67
00:02:27,171 --> 00:02:28,225
Remember this.

68
00:02:28,225 --> 00:02:31,062
Classify by the body, not by the address.

69
00:02:31,062 --> 00:02:32,579
Feathers make a bird.

70
00:02:32,579 --> 00:02:34,046
Milk makes a mammal.

71
00:02:34,646 --> 00:02:36,263
Now, a worked example.

72
00:02:36,263 --> 00:02:38,674
Four animals with fish in their name.

73
00:02:38,674 --> 00:02:40,396
Which ones are real fish?

74
00:02:40,746 --> 00:02:42,501
Asterias, the star fish.

75
00:02:42,501 --> 00:02:46,647
Spiny skin, and it lives in the
sea, but it has no backbone.

76
00:02:46,647 --> 00:02:48,108
It is an echinoderm.

77
00:02:48,558 --> 00:02:50,427
Aurelia, the jelly fish.

78
00:02:50,427 --> 00:02:52,735
A soft body with stinging cells.

79
00:02:52,735 --> 00:02:54,447
It belongs to Cnidaria.

80
00:02:54,897 --> 00:02:56,577
Sepia, the cuttle fish.

81
00:02:56,577 --> 00:02:59,406
A soft body, with its shell hidden inside.

82
00:02:59,406 --> 00:03:00,651
It is a mollusc.

83
00:03:01,101 --> 00:03:03,007
Scoliodon, the dog fish.

84
00:03:03,007 --> 00:03:05,893
Cartilage skeleton, fins and gill slits.

85
00:03:05,893 --> 00:03:08,257
The only real fish of the four.

86
00:03:08,907 --> 00:03:10,372
Now, the exam trap.

87
00:03:10,722 --> 00:03:13,591
Many students say mammals never lay eggs.

88
00:03:13,991 --> 00:03:17,121
But the platypus lays eggs
and is still a mammal.

89
00:03:17,121 --> 00:03:19,890
Mammals are viviparous
with a few exceptions.

90
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:21,914
Where is this asked?

91
00:03:21,914 --> 00:03:26,146
As match the following: a genus with
its class, or an odd example with

92
00:03:26,146 --> 00:03:27,046
its feature.

93
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,886
Exam level now.

94
00:03:28,886 --> 00:03:32,189
Which genus is correctly
matched with its class?

95
00:03:32,189 --> 00:03:33,488
Pause and solve.

96
00:03:38,888 --> 00:03:40,226
The answer is B.

97
00:03:40,226 --> 00:03:43,423
Exocoetus, the flying
fish, is a bony fish.

98
00:03:43,923 --> 00:03:45,666
Aptenodytes is the penguin.

99
00:03:45,666 --> 00:03:47,675
It is a bird, not a mammal.

100
00:03:48,175 --> 00:03:51,279
Ornithorhynchus lays
eggs, but it is a mammal.

101
00:03:51,279 --> 00:03:54,630
Ichthyophis is a limbless
amphibian, not a reptile.

102
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:56,690
Here is your recap.

103
00:03:56,690 --> 00:03:58,192
Screenshot this card.

104
00:04:01,392 --> 00:04:04,228
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

105
00:04:04,628 --> 00:04:05,528
One.

106
00:04:05,134 --> 00:04:07,809
Why is a bat a mammal and not a bird?

107
00:04:08,709 --> 00:04:09,609
Two.

108
00:04:09,258 --> 00:04:11,024
Which mammal lays eggs?

109
00:04:11,924 --> 00:04:12,824
Three.

110
00:04:12,583 --> 00:04:14,431
Is a star fish a fish?

111
00:04:14,431 --> 00:04:15,331
Why not?

112
00:04:16,363 --> 00:04:20,688
Next time: one flowchart that
sorts every animal in this chapter.

113
00:04:20,688 --> 00:04:22,049
Can you build it?

114
00:04:22,049 --> 00:04:25,318
We find out in comparative
classification diagrams.
